  "limits": [
    "Native Linux feature required. Finite curves with common-sign nonzero weights; one-million-control output net plus existing transfer/crease limits. Rail start radius must exceed model tolerance.",
    "Rational/spatial profiles, arbitrary/reversed/remote axes, independent parameter domains, closed rails and unclamped input bases are covered. Native surface charts are preserved independently of Rhino chart orientation.",
    "ScaleHeight requires endpoint-clamped active bases; public SDK diagnostic observations show unmatched unclamped rational-quadratic behavior. The combination is rejected before native construction or document mutation.",
    "ScaleHeight falls back to axial translation at absolute reference heights <=2^-26, including zero. Boundary behavior is based on four public SDK observations and a native regression test.",
    "SplitAtTangents=Yes splits native classified kink and tangent joins; No retains a single tensor surface. Native B-rep shared-edge and pole handling is tested locally; Rhino split topology is not qualified.",
    "Twelve complete stored rational fixture surfaces have continuous geometric distance bounds <=1e-6. The positive rational tensor partition bounds control displacement and weight ratio oscillation after chart alignment. These are fixture-specific certificates, not a runtime acceptance proof for arbitrary inputs.",
    "Three hundred closest-point output comparisons use 2e-6 model units; area comparisons use 1e-5 square model units. The closest-point allowance includes solver and evaluation roundoff at a 3e9 world origin; no relative coordinate tolerance is used.",
    "Reference uses the public NurbsSurface.CreateRailRevolvedSurface API with private curve copies. Rhino native command getter, split topology, metadata, associative history and performance parity remain unqualified.",
    "AddressSanitizer instruments the complete SMLib, SM_API and adapter archives. Rust and separately bundled dependencies are not separately instrumented; leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks are disabled.",
    "3 historical qualification records preserve source hashes through immutable Git references; their non-hash fields remain unchanged. Pre-existing unverifiable records are untouched."
  ],
